CHAPTER 2 — Introduction to Software Development Workflow

Lesson 01: Software Development Workflow (12:18)
Notes:
Project team consists of:
- Product Owner = Identifies the product requirements by talking to the customer. Translates these requirements to the team. Figures out how and what the app should look like/do.
- Software Developer = Program the application.
- Tester = Test the application
- Systems Administrator = Create and configure the sever and make the application accessible to the users. Manage and administer database, configure networking for servers.

Collaboration is important.

Communication between all team members allow for tasks and requirements to be defined clearly.

Jira Software helps keep track of issues and project progress.
- Widely used in software development teams.
- An essential tool.
- In every IT project you will be using Jira

Agile
- A philosophy with core set of values or principles.

Scrum (Framework)
- One of the most popular frameworks.

Lesson 02: What is Agile and Scrum (19:53)
Notes:
Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC)

Programming:

- Software is programmed by developers
- One team per app or per feature depending on the scale of the project
- Create new functions and fix bugs

Software Testing:

- Test the new features
- Test the old code/functionality
- Testing is done by developers or dedicated testers
- Automated testing

Operations:

- Run software in production (on code that's already running)
- Build application and run on servers (upgrade existing software)

Waterfall vs Agile:

Traditional Waterfall:
1) Requirements = plan everything beforehand
2) Developments = developers code complete app
3) Testing = testing after everything has been deployed
4) Operations = huge preparation

The stages in this development cycle take months, proving to be extremely innefficient.
Overtime new requirements may arise.
Many places of failure and miscommunication.

Agile Software Development:

Benefits:
- Each feature gets tested and deployed
- Immediate feedback
- Fast and flexible development and deployment process
- Scrum & Kanban (specific implementations)

What is Agile? 

Develop the application with continuous, short iterations (and several phases)
Teams cycle through a process of planning, executing and evluating.
Easier and faster and cheaper to make adjustments during development (flexibility)
Delivers product in small, but consumable increments.
Requirements, plans and results are all evaluated continuously.
Enables the team to respond to feedback quickly.

Continuous collaboration with team members and the customers

Scrum:

Sprints: The duration of the actual iteration process (typically 2-3 weeks but could vary up to 1-4 weeks based on the projects needs)

Goal is to build the most important features first.

Feedback from previous sprints are used as input for upcoming sprints.

Sprint Planning:
- Prioritize tasks since you cannot work on all of it at once.
- The list of prioritized requirements is called a backlog.
- Backlog is flexible, things could be added, removed, or changed.

Scrum Roles:

- Scrum Master: ensures thet scrum is done properly by the team, guides and facilitates, responsible for holding meetings.
- Product Owner: represents the customer's interests, add or removes or changes backlog, prioritizes tasks on a regular basis.
- Scrum Team: self organized team, consists of programmers, testers, designers, system admins, etc. Shares responsibility for meeting the sprints goal.

Other Stakeholders:
Management and people from the customer side.

JIRA Software used for scrum and project management.

