CHAPTER 3 — Web Development with HTML, CSS and JavaScript

Lesson 01: How Websites Work (9:21)
Notes:

- Files of the website "live" in California but temporarily live in your laptop. Travels from CA to your computer.

Frontend:
- HTML: Text, image, link, no style no swagger
- CSS: Styling of a webpage, features colors, fonts, positioning
- Javascript: The functionality of the website. Everything you interact with.

Backend:
- "Lives" in the back
- Makes data available to others.
- Keeps history of data.
- Can be written in different languages
- Validates the received data.

Database:
- Like a warehouse for data. Stores messages, comments, likes, etc.
- Servers run 24/7 to be availabe to everyone at all times. Serves applications to people.

Web Developer can work on all three components but to specialize in one you would be either a frontend developer, backend developer, or a database engineer.

